{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && sed -n '550,620p' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n\nscope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\napplies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n\n## Task 1: prepare and launch finite-fiber and stabilizer-hyperfinite queues\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Aristotle, Codex, `aristotle_autopilot.py`, autopilot.toml, FF15–FF23, P37–P46, `AUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes`, `AUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance`, AUTONOMY_POLICY.md\n\n## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- systemd, `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN`, `<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`, `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`, quarantine snapshot, `.lake`, `lake build`, state.json\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user said Aristotle may “develop necessary theory” or take “another easier route” -> permit project-local supporting theory and alternative recognizable proofs, but require explicit assumptions and no silent weakening [Task 1]\n- when the user requested copying only `main.tex` and bibliography -> stage only `manuscript/main.tex`, `manuscript/references.bib`, and `manuscript/mainNotes.bib`, not the whole Overleaf tree [Task 1]\n- when the user asked to “append the endgame packets and start the loop” -> carry theorem-target packets through the requested endgame rather than stopping at conditional infrastructure interfaces [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n- Upload staging contains the Lean project, the three approved manuscript files, and `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`; the policy forbids `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, and silent weakening. [Task 1]\n- The user systemd timer polls every five minutes. For NVM installation, the service and Python resolution need explicit `PATH` and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`; this run verified `codex-cli 0.146.0`. [Task 2]\n- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- symptom: systemd reports `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'` and terminal Aristotle jobs never close out -> cause: the NVM executable is outside noninteractive PATH -> fix: set the absolute Codex path in both the service and runner, then verify the service environment. [Task 2]\n- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n- status guard: at rollout end FF15 and P37 were still active. Do not claim candidate acceptance, FF15 integration, or FF16/P38 submission until `state.json`, closeout output/review, and live Lean checks agree. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: <original-home>/Projects/current/ml_engineer ML research direction, causal toy-Transformer, and quantum-chemistry RL planning\n\nscope: choose small independently verifiable ML-for-science or alignment projects, explain the scientific object before implementation, and preserve evaluator-first boundaries\napplies_to: cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/ml_engineer; reuse_rule=reuse as planning/lesson guidance, not as an implemented system; inspect current `AGENTS.md` locations, worktree state, APIs, and library conventions before creating artifacts\n\n## Task 1: choose a benchmarkable ML-for-science research direction\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-04T07-51-57-TxZz-ml_research_frontiers_project_direction.md (cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/ml_engineer, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T09-51-57-019fcbc2-049f-79d1-bb0f-e96c645000c5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T07:53:35+00:00, thread_id=019fcbc2-049f-79d1-bb0f-e96c645000c5, success: candidate projects and validation criteria scoped)\n\n### keywords\n\n- neural quantum states, transverse-field Ising, exact diagonalization, NetKet, scaffold split, TDC, OC20, OC22, energy error, Hamiltonian variance\n\n## Task 2: orient a mechanistic-interpretability project around causal tests\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-04T08-00-33-zl46-alignment_mechanistic_interpretability_project_orientation.md (cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/ml_engineer, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/04/rollout-2026-08-04T10-00-33-019fcbc9-e137-7813-a454-403391d2e68a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T08:01:26+00:00, thread_id=019fcbc9-e137-7813-a454-403391d2e68a, success: causal toy-Transformer project selected; no files changed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- mechanistic-interpretability, alignment, TinyTransformer, synthetic modular arithmetic, activation patching, ablation, compositional generalization, adversarial format, process supervision\n\n## Task 3: formulate active-space molecular Hamiltonian RL discovery\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' PLAN.md\nsed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P57C-pure-gns-type-one-factor.md\nrg --files -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'state.json' -g 'SOURCE-CONTRACT.md' -g 'CONTEXT-LEDGER.md' -g 'AUTONOMY_POLICY.md' -g 'P57*-closeout.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' PLAN.md\nsed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P57C-pure-gns-type-one-factor.md\nrg --files -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*STATUS*' -g 'state.json' -g 'SOURCE-CONTRACT.md' -g 'CONTEXT-LEDGER.md' -g 'AUTONOMY_POLICY.md' -g 'P57*-closeout.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# Active plan: two-lane stabilizer-algebra formalization\n\n## Decision — 2026-08-07\n\nThe project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\nstabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\nsilently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n\n### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n\nFor a general consistent stabilizer system and region, construct the decreasing\nlocal-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\ntracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\nand derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n\nThis lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\nseparate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\nof a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\nmerely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n\n### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n\nFrom a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\ntheir coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\nmodels, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\nthe special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n\n`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n\nAfter proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\ntrivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\nnot follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\nspatial factorization.\n\n### Reconnection\n\nLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\nconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\nthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\nthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\nthe two results remain logically independent.\n\n## Aristotle package sequence\n\n### Shared/central core\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n\n### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Retired partial result: it proves the finite-word/algebraic state equality and conditional continuous-extension uniqueness, but does not prove C-star boundedness or positivity. |\n| P56R | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Recovery after P55D: construct the pure/mixed product C-star state from finite-dimensional density-matrix estimates, prove positivity/unitality and transport it through `alpha`; no supplied norm bound. |\n| P57A | `VacuumRestrictedInfiniteTensorProduct.lean` | Shared infrastructure: port and audit the proved finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite-tensor pre-Hilbert core from `bound_beating`; do not import external projects or package a completion as an axiom. |\n| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | After P54, P56R, and P57A, construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Retired partial transport artifact: it compiles conditional centre/trace/weight transports but introduces unproved bridge and local-normality premises, so it is not evidence for the Lane-H theorem. |\n| P59A | `ConcretePureMixedProductData.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed coordinate C-star subalgebras, their commuting dense product decomposition, and the concrete `ProductGNSData` instance directly from P55D/P56R. |\n| P57B | `VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion.lean` | Starting from P57A's proved finite-support core, construct the null-space quotient/completion as an actual Hilbert space with dense algebraic embedding; no completed ITP interface may be assumed. |\n| P57C | `PureGNSFactor.lean` | Identify the concrete pure component of P59A with the P57B vacuum product representation and prove its represented von Neumann closure is the full `B(K_pure)` factor. |\n| P59B | `MixedGNSUHFBridge.lean` | Identify P59A's mixed GNS representation with P58's dyadic-UHF model and transport its factor/tracial structure; no fresh mixed-factor premise. |\n| P59R | `RegionalFactorTransport.lean` | Combine P57, P57C, and P59B to identify the regional represented algebra with the concrete spatial product and prove trivial centre/factorhood. |\n| P59T | `RegionalTraceWeight.lean` | Separately prove the finite-pure tracial-state and infinite-pure semifinite-weight results using a standard ultraweak-normal interface; never use P59's local vector-normal predicates as substitutes. |\n\n### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n\n## Initial parallel wave\n\nSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\nand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   traciality and faithfulness.\n8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   integrated and audited.\n9. P56 is preserved as a partial artifact, not accepted evidence: its\n   `ProductStateBound` is an explicit missing C-star norm estimate and it has\n   no positivity theorem. P56R must derive the bound and positivity from the\n   finite-dimensional density-matrix data and P55D's concrete C-star model;\n   it may not use `ProductStateBound` in its final declarations or proofs.\n10. P57A may reuse the algorithmic finite-support construction in\n    `bound_beating/formalize_itp`, but only by an audited local port. It may\n    not import that separate project, copy its optional completion/axiom\n    wrappers, or claim a completed Hilbert tensor product before the quotient\n    and completion API is actually proved.\n11. P59 is a preserved partial transport artifact, not an accepted theorem.\n    P59A must construct, rather than assume, the `ProductGNSData` used by P57;\n    P59B must connect that datum to P58's `mixedVonNeumann`; and P57C must\n    establish the pure type-I factor. P59R may use only those proved bridges.\n    The finite/infinite trace conclusions are separated into P59T, where the\n    normality predicate must be standard ultraweak normality and the infinite\n    branch must carry an explicit infinitude hypothesis.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n\n1. Split coordinate indices into pure and mixed sectors.\n2. Establish the infinite-product GNS factorization.\n3. Identify the pure sector as `B(K_pure)`.\n4. Identify the mixed sector as a finite matrix factor when finite, or the\nhyperfinite `II_1` factor when infinite.\n5. Establish the spatial tensor-product identification of the product\nrepresentation.\n\n**Gate D:** every analytic theorem is either formalized against a supported\nMathlib API or recorded as an exact external theorem with source locator and\nexplicit hypothesis.\n\n## Phase E — theorem and trace corollaries\n\n1. Transport the Phase-D product classification through the Phase-C GNS\nunitary to the regional von Neumann algebra.\n2. State the finite-pure and infinite-pure cases separately.\n3. Finite pure sector: derive the normalized tracial-state conclusion.\n4. Infinite pure sector: state the faithful normal semifinite trace/weight\nconclusion; do not call it a tracial state.\n5. Audit every conclusion against `main.tex:1740-1752` and record any required\nmanuscript correction separately.\n\n## Parallelization\n\nUntil Phase B is blocked on a single coherent-coordinate construction, run in\nparallel:\n\n- finite phase/cocycle verification;\n- finite adapted-coordinate/stabilizer-state verification;\n- finite inclusion/coherence lemmas;\n- Mathlib/API feasibility audits for C-star inductive limits and GNS products;\n- product mixed-sector classification/source work.\n\nDo not parallelize mutually dependent attempts at the same global `alpha`.\nEach new Aristotle packet must use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` and state its\nsource basis plus every auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Exit criterion\n\nCall the manuscript theorem formally established only when Gates A--D are\ndischarged and Phase E compiles without substituting supplied interfaces for\nthe central finite-coordinate, C-star-extension, state-identity, or\nproduct-classification claims.\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-10: P56 is retained as a partial, reviewed artifact. Its\nfinite-word and algebraic direct-limit identities are useful, but its concrete\nextensions depend on `ProductStateBound` and no positivity theorem was proved.\nP56R replaces it as the Lane-H state gate and must derive a genuine unital\npositive C-star functional directly from the finite pure/mixed density-matrix\ndata and the P55D concrete alpha. The original P56 job is disabled rather than\nrewritten, so the distinction remains machine-visible.\n\nIn parallel, P57A ports the *proved* finite-support vacuum-restricted infinite\ntensor pre-Hilbert construction from the compatible Lean-4.28 `bound_beating`\nworkspace into this repository as shared infrastructure. This is a local port,\nnot a cross-project import. Its optional completion/axiom wrapper is explicitly\nexcluded: P57A can establish the algebraic kernel, finite-mode realization,\npositivity, sesquilinearity, and pre-inner-product core, but the completed\nHilbert-space and spatial tensor claims remain P57 work and must be proved\nagainst the local Mathlib API.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-10: P59 is retained only as an audited partial artifact.\nIt restated P57's generic transport but did not construct a `ProductGNSData`\nfrom the P55D/P56R local-hyperbolic model, did not identify that datum's mixed\nGNS representation with P58's `mixedVonNeumann`, and replaced the required\nfactor and trace inputs with fresh premise bundles. The recovery is therefore\nsplit into proof gates: P59A constructs the concrete product datum; P57B\nconstructs the actual Hilbert completion of the P57A vacuum core; P57C proves\nthe pure type-I factor; P59B proves the mixed-UHF bridge; and P59R transports\nthe resulting factorization to the regional algebra. P59T treats traces and\nweights only after P59R, using standard ultraweak normality and an explicit\ninfinite-pure hypothesis for the weight branch.\n# P57C — pure GNS type-I factor\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1945-1963`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P57C`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** P59A and P57B, integrated and locally audited.\n- **Gate discharged:** identify the constructed pure coordinate GNS\n  representation with the vacuum ITP and prove its represented closure is the\n  full type-I operator factor.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no mixed-UHF identification, no regional\n  factor transport, and no trace/weight conclusion.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/PureGNSFactor.lean`. Instantiate P59A's pure\ncoordinate state and P57B's completed vacuum ITP. Construct the canonical GNS\nunitary, prove the finite-word action agrees with finite excitations, and prove\nthe bicommutant of the pure represented coordinate algebra is the full bounded\noperator algebra on the completed pure space. Derive trivial centre from that\nequality.\n\nNo `pure_factor`, `pure_commutant`, GNS-unitary, or `B(K)`-closure premise may\nbe introduced. If pinned Mathlib lacks an essential theorem, prove it locally\nor report the exact gap without accepting the package.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nOnly the integrated P59A coordinate assumptions and P57B vacuum construction.\nState finite/infinite coordinate branches explicitly.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/PureGNSFactor.lean`; import P59A, P57B, and\nthe existing bicommutant infrastructure.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.PureGNSFactor` succeeds without `sorry`,\naxiom, supplied pure-factor premise, mixed claim, or trace/weight conclusion.\nCONTEXT-LEDGER.md\nSOURCE-CONTRACT.md\nreviews/P57-product-gns-tensor-factorization-closeout.md\nreviews/P57A-vacuum-restricted-itp-core-closeout.md\nreviews/P57B-vacuum-itp-completion-closeout.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
