{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md\nrg -n 'GNS|ITP|unitary|surject|completion|elemVec|inner_elemVec|vonNeumannGenerated|commutant_eq_scalar' AristotleCandidates/PureGNSFactor.lean\nsed -n '1,220p' reviews/P59A-concrete-pure-mixed-product-data-closeout.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review Protocol\n\nUse this before closing substantive Codex work. The goal is to find defects, not\nto summarize accomplishments.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Identify the artifact types touched: `code`, `math`, `tex`, `computation`,\n   `source-backed`, `workflow`.\n2. Inspect the diff or new artifact against the user's request.\n3. Report findings by severity first. If there are no findings, say so and state\n   the remaining risk.\n\n## Universal Checks\n\n- Did the work answer the actual latest user request?\n- Did it modify unrelated files or broaden scope?\n- Did it overwrite, reformat, or revert pre-existing user changes?\n- Are generated files, caches, logs, plots, PDFs, or build artifacts handled\n  intentionally?\n- Are final claims stronger than the evidence supports?\n- Are verification commands actually relevant to the changed artifact?\n\n## Code Checks\n\n- Does the changed behavior match the stated interface and edge cases?\n- Are tests missing for a changed behavior, bug fix, parser, numerical routine,\n  CLI command, or user-facing workflow?\n- Are errors handled where inputs, files, network calls, or external tools can\n  fail?\n- Is there hidden global state, path sensitivity, nondeterminism, race risk, or\n  stale cache behavior?\n- Did dependency, config, or environment changes alter unrelated workflows?\n\n## Math Checks\n\n- Are all assumptions, domains, signs, conventions, normalizations, and boundary\n  conditions stated before use?\n- Are definitions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n2:import AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion\n7:# P57C — the pure coordinate GNS representation is the full type-I factor\n15:  (`AristotleCandidates.VacuumRestrictedITPCompletion`), both integrated, together with the\n17:* Gate discharged: identify the constructed pure coordinate GNS representation with the vacuum\n27:vacuum construction.  No `pure_factor`, `pure_commutant`, GNS-unitary or `B(K)`-closure premise\n36:namespace PureGNSFactor\n248:/-! ## 3. The pure GNS representation -/\n255:/-- **The pure GNS Hilbert space**: the GNS space of the P59A pure marginal state. -/\n256:noncomputable abbrev PureGNS := R.purePositiveState.GNS\n265:theorem norm_toPreGNS_le (a : R.pureCStar) :\n266:    ‖(R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)‖ ≤ 1 * ‖a‖ := by\n267:  have h := PositiveLinearMap.preGNS_norm_sq (f := R.purePositiveState)\n268:    (R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)\n269:  have h2 : ‖(R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)‖ ^ 2 ≤ ‖a‖ ^ 2 := by\n270:    have hre : ((‖(R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ)\n273:    calc (‖(R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ)\n274:        = ‖((‖(R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a)‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ)‖ := by\n282:/-- **The canonical map of the pure algebra into its GNS space.** -/\n283:noncomputable def gvecL : R.pureCStar →L[ℂ] PureGNS R :=\n285:    (LinearMap.mkContinuous (R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS.toLinearMap) 1 (norm_toPreGNS_le R))\n288:    gvecL R a = ((R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a : R.purePositiveState.PreGNS) : PureGNS R) := rfl\n290:/-- **The GNS vacuum vector** of the pure coordinate state. -/\n291:noncomputable def vac : PureGNS R := gvecL R 1\n295:/-- **The GNS representation** of the pure coordinate C⋆-algebra. -/\n296:noncomputable abbrev pureRep : R.pureCStar →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) :=\n302:    PositiveLinearMap.preGNS_inner_def]\n330:  have h : Set.range (gvecL R) = Set.range ((↑) : R.purePositiveState.PreGNS → PureGNS R) := by\n333:    · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩; exact ⟨R.purePositiveState.toPreGNS a, rfl⟩\n334:    · rintro ⟨p, rfl⟩; exact ⟨R.purePositiveState.ofPreGNS p, rfl⟩\n365:/-- **The vacuum projection fixes the GNS vacuum vector.** -/\n406:/-! ## 5. Irreducibility of the pure GNS representation -/\n408:/-- The GNS vectors of the pure Pauli words. -/\n409:def wordVecs : Set (PureGNS R) :=\n454:/-- **The GNS vectors of the pure Pauli words span a dense subspace of the pure GNS space.** -/\n456:    Dense ((Submodule.span ℂ (wordVecs R) : Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R)) := by\n457:  have himg : ⇑(gvecL R : R.pureCStar →ₗ[ℂ] PureGNS R) '' pureWordSet R = wordVecs R :=\n459:  have hmap : Submodule.map (gvecL R : R.pureCStar →ₗ[ℂ] PureGNS R)\n463:      closure ((Submodule.span ℂ (wordVecs R) : Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R)) := by\n474:        = ((Submodule.span ℂ (wordVecs R) : Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R)) := by\n484:/-- Any closed submodule containing the GNS word vectors is everything. -/\n485:theorem eq_top_of_wordVecs_subset (p : Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R))\n486:    (hp : IsClosed (p : Set (PureGNS R))) (hsub : wordVecs R ⊆ (p : Set (PureGNS R))) :\n487:    (p : Set (PureGNS R)) = Set.univ := by\n488:  have hle : ((Submodule.span ℂ (wordVecs R) : Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R))\n489:      ⊆ (p : Set (PureGNS R)) := fun _ hx => (Submodule.span_le.mpr hsub) hx\n494:theorem eq_zero_of_inner_wordVecs {z : PureGNS R}\n496:  have hker : ((LinearMap.ker ((innerSL ℂ z : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] ℂ) : PureGNS R →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n497:      Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R)) = Set.univ := by\n502:  have hz : z ∈ (LinearMap.ker ((innerSL ℂ z : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] ℂ) : PureGNS R →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n503:      Submodule ℂ (PureGNS R)) := by\n508:/-- A vector orthogonal to every GNS word vector vanishes (second-slot form). -/\n509:theorem eq_zero_of_inner_wordVecs' {z : PureGNS R}\n516:theorem eq_zero_of_apply_wordVecs {S : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R}\n518:  have hker : ((LinearMap.ker (S : PureGNS R →ₗ[ℂ] PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R)) = Set.univ := by\n523:  have hx : x ∈ (LinearMap.ker (S : PureGNS R →ₗ[ℂ] PureGNS R)) := by\n528:theorem inner_pureRep_left (a : R.pureCStar) (u z : PureGNS R) :\n532:  have h3 := congrArg (fun S : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R => ⟪u, S z⟫_ℂ) hstar\n535:/-- Multiplicativity of the pure GNS representation, in applied form. -/\n536:theorem pureRep_mul_apply (a b : R.pureCStar) (u : PureGNS R) :\n538:  congrArg (fun S : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R => S u) (map_mul (pureRep R) a b)\n542:commuting operator `T` between the GNS vectors of `x` and `y` is `lam` times their inner\n544:theorem inner_commutant_of_absorb {T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R}\n545:    (hcomm : ∀ (a : R.pureCStar) (u : PureGNS R), pureRep R a (T u) = T (pureRep R a u))\n610:theorem inner_word_commutant {T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R}\n611:    (hcomm : ∀ (a : R.pureCStar) (u : PureGNS R), pureRep R a (T u) = T (pureRep R a u))\n623:theorem inner_sub_scalar_apply (T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) (lam : ℂ) (u z : PureGNS R) :\n624:    ⟪u, (T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) z⟫_ℂ\n629:/-- If all matrix elements of `T` between GNS word vectors are `lam` times the corresponding\n631:theorem eq_smul_one_of_word_matrix {T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R} (lam : ℂ)\n637:    T = lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) := by\n639:      (T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) u = 0 := by\n649:          (T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) (gvecL R (pureWordP R w hw))⟫_ℂ\n651:          (T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) (gvecL R (pureWordP R w' hwp))⟫_ℂ :=\n653:        (T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) (gvecL R q)⟫_ℂ) hxv hxw\n656:  have hTS : T - lam • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) = 0 :=\n661:/-- **Irreducibility of the pure GNS representation.**  Every bounded operator commuting with\n663:theorem commutant_eq_scalar {T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R}\n665:    T = (⟪vac R, T (vac R)⟫_ℂ) • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) := by\n666:  have hcomm : ∀ (a : R.pureCStar) (u : PureGNS R),\n669:    have h2 := congrArg (fun f : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R => f u) (hT a)\n677:on the pure GNS space. -/\n678:noncomputable def pureVN : StarSubalgebra ℂ (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) :=\n681:theorem mem_pureVN_iff {T : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R} :\n685:    pureRep R a ∈ ((pureVN R : StarSubalgebra ℂ (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) :\n686:      Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) := ⟨a, rfl⟩\n688:/-- The scalar operators on the pure GNS space. -/\n689:def scalarOps : Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) :=\n690:  {T | ∃ c : ℂ, T = c • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)}\n693:    c • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) ∈ scalarOps R := ⟨c, rfl⟩\n695:theorem scalar_comm (c : ℂ) (y : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) :\n696:    y * (c • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) = (c • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) * y := by\n697:  have h : (c • (1 : PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R))\n698:      = algebraMap ℂ (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R) c :=\n706:    Set.centralizer ((pureVN R : StarSubalgebra ℂ (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) :\n707:      Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) = scalarOps R := by\n713:      commutant_eq_scalar R (fun a => hT _ (pureRep_mem_pureVN R a))⟩\n719:    Set.centralizer (scalarOps R) = (Set.univ : Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) := by\n726:theorem coe_vonNeumannGenerated_pureVN :\n727:    ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated (pureVN R) :\n728:        VonNeumannAlgebra (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) = Set.univ := by\n729:  rw [StarSubalgebra.coe_vonNeumannGenerated, centralizer_pureVN, centralizer_scalarOps]\n731:/-- **The pure GNS representation generates the type-I factor `B(K)`**, in the form of an\n733:theorem vonNeumannGenerated_pureVN_eq_top :\n734:    (StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated (pureVN R)).toStarSubalgebra\n735:      = (⊤ : StarSubalgebra ℂ (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R)) := by\n738:  exact coe_vonNeumannGenerated_pureVN R\n742:theorem centre_vonNeumannGenerated_pureVN :\n743:    ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated (pureVN R) :\n744:        VonNeumannAlgebra (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R))\n745:      ∩ Set.centralizer ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated (pureVN R) :\n746:        VonNeumannAlgebra (PureGNS R)) : Set (PureGNS R →L[ℂ] PureGNS R))\n748:  rw [StarSubalgebra.centralizer_vonNeumannGenerated, centralizer_pureVN,\n749:    coe_vonNeumannGenerated_pureVN, Set.univ_inter]\n751:/-! ## 7. The pure GNS space is the vacuum infinite tensor product\n754:GNS space should be the vacuum-restricted infinite tensor product of one qubit per selected\n798:/-- **The GNS vector of a pure coordinate word**, independent of any stage choice. -/\n799:noncomputable def wordVec (c : PauliCoordinateLabels I) (hc : A.IsPureLabel c) : PureGNS R :=\n937:/-- **The GNS vector of the `X`-word** on a finite set of selected modes: the finite excitation\n939:noncomputable def xVec (T : Finset (Mode A)) : PureGNS R :=\n956:open VacuumRestrictedITP\n961:infinite-tensor-product data is instantiated at this family.  The map `elemVec` sends a\n963:excitations in the pure GNS space, and it reproduces the P57A kernel exactly. -/\n1007:noncomputable def elemVecOn (v : VacuumTensor (vacQ A)) (S : Finset (Mode A)) : PureGNS R :=\n1030:theorem elemVecOn_mono {v : VacuumTensor (vacQ A)} {S S' : Finset (Mode A)}\n1031:    (hv : v.active ⊆ S) (hSS' : S ⊆ S') : elemVecOn R v S' = elemVecOn R v S := by\n1033:  rw [elemVecOn, elemVecOn]\n1040:/-- **The pure GNS vector attached to a vacuum-restricted elementary tensor.** -/\n1041:noncomputable def elemVec (v : VacuumTensor (vacQ A)) : PureGNS R := elemVecOn R v v.active\n1043:theorem elemVec_eq_elemVecOn {v : VacuumTensor (vacQ A)} {S : Finset (Mode A)}\n1044:    (hv : v.active ⊆ S) : elemVec R v = elemVecOn R v S :=\n1045:  (elemVecOn_mono R (Finset.Subset.refl _) hv).symm\n1079:theorem inner_elemVec (v w : VacuumTensor (vacQ A)) :\n1080:    ⟪elemVec R v, elemVec R w⟫_ℂ = kern v w := by\n1084:  rw [elemVec_eq_elemVecOn R hv, elemVec_eq_elemVecOn R hw, elemVecOn, elemVecOn,\n1087:end PureGNSFactor\n# P59A closeout review — concrete pure/mixed product datum\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the packet's stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nAristotle task `f17ae380-7cbe-4e16-8ea3-94d98cb8ef47` is terminal `COMPLETE` in `history/logs/20260810T213056Z-a130d169-tasks.log`. Only its exact archive `aristotle_responses/P59A-concrete-pure-mixed-product-data-a130d169-f17ae380.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `54d09cdca8580fdc5a2d1d37f4db6f4d805e6f46e93acc4fa9db58e33d9ce75b`) was extracted into its named quarantine directory. No build, dependency update, or fetch was run there. The only integrated source is the packet-authorized `AristotleCandidates/ConcretePureMixedProductData.lean`. Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values agree:\n\n```text\n8e646687234146d34a1e27c63eb8c65ddbe9cfc59a025135291e9a932a34b8b6\n```\n\nThe quarantined copies of `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`, `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`, and `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` are byte-identical to their live, locally audited counterparts. P57 is used only for its already integrated `ProductGNSData` structure.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `A : AlphaData L I` and `R : A.SourceConcreteRep`, P59A constructs:\n\n- `pureCStar`, `mixedCStar`, `pureEmbedding`, and `mixedEmbedding` as the closed selected-coordinate and complementary-coordinate C-star subalgebras of `R.sourceCStar` and their inclusion star homomorphisms;\n- `pureCStar_mixedCStar_commute` and `pureEmbedding_mixedEmbedding_commute`, derived by closing the verified cross-coordinate Pauli-word commutation relation;\n- `productSpan` and `dense_productSpan`, using the exact split of every finite-stage word and the P55D dense source embedding;\n- `totalStateCLM_mul`, which factors the recovered P56R source state on all pure/mixed elementary products; and\n- the square-positivity conversion `positiveOfStarSq`, positive marginals, `SourceConcreteRep.concreteProductGNSData`, and the branch-uniform `AlphaData.concreteProductGNSData`, with identification lemmas for the total algebra and total state.\n\nThere is no new premise argument. The result inherits only the explicit coordinate-model data already carried by `AlphaData` and `SourceConcreteRep`: the accepted P52/P53/P55D coordinate and concrete-model data, including the named `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` fields. The total state is exactly P56R's `cstarProductStateRecovered`; `ProductStateBound` is not an argument of any P59A declaration. The C-star order used to build Mathlib `PositiveLinearMap`s is explicitly `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`.\n\n## Acceptance classification\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The selected/complementary concrete C-star subalgebras, commuting inclusions, norm-dense span of their elementary products, positive unital marginal functionals, product identity, contractivity, and concrete `ProductGNSData` are constructed from P55D/P56R data. |\n| partial | The result is conditional infrastructure relative to the manuscript: it does not construct the underlying local-hyperbolic coordinate/model hypotheses from `main.tex:1925-1967`. |\n| blocked | Completed ITP/GNS factor identification, pure and mixed factor classification, regional factor transport, and trace/weight conclusions remain separate downstream gates. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThus P59A's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. This is not a proof of a completed infinite tensor product, a factor theorem, or a trace/weight theorem.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P59A`, Lane `H`, as declared in both the packet and `PLAN.md`.\n- **Predecessors:** P55D and P56R are integrated, live audited in their respective closeouts, and match the quarantined copies. The integrated P57 supplies only the generic target structure permitted by the packet; it is not used to obtain a factor or trace conclusion.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: P59A instantiates P57's generic product datum from the P55D/P56R concrete coordinate model rather than adding arbitrary `ProductGNSData`, density, product-state, positivity, or norm-bound fields.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no completed ITP, pure/mixed factor classification, regional factor, normality, trace, or weight theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.ConcretePureMixedProductData` — completed, but Lake has no registered target for this untracked candidate and produced no candidate `.olean`; it is not acceptance evidence by itself.\n- `lake env lean AristotleCandidates/ConcretePureMixedProductData.lean` — passed in the live project; this is the narrow source-level Lean check.\n- Direct live elaboration of P59A together with `#print axioms` for `pureCStar_mixedCStar_commute`, `dense_productSpan`, `totalStateCLM_mul`, `positiveOfStarSq`, both exported datum declarations, and the non-vacuity theorem — passed. Each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Direct live Lean checks of the P55D, P56R, and P57 support modules — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed (existing registered project targets up to date).\n- Declaration-head scan of P59A — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking issue found. The load-bearing checks were that each finite source word is split into pure and mixed filters at the same stage, the two pairing orientations vanish before commutation is concluded, dense span follows from the actual P55D dense source embedding, and state factorization is extended from words only through closed linear submodules. The positivity conversion explicitly uses the pinned spectral C-star order; it does not replace positivity by an axiom. Compilation and axiom reports validate the Lean artifact, not the inherited coordinate hypotheses or later operator-algebraic claims.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P59A candidate, its exact archive, quarantine extraction, and this review. All pre-existing modified and untracked plan, packet, candidate, and review files were preserved. No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, archive build, dependency update, or dependency fetch occurred.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
